# Build context is the repo root for both images (docker build -f
# backend/Dockerfile . and -f frontend/Dockerfile ., see docker-compose*.yml).
# Allow list: `*` excludes everything, then one `!` entry per path the two
# Dockerfiles read, so a file dropped anywhere else in the checkout (a key, a
# dump, an agent scratch dir, docs) never reaches the daemon. The entries mirror
# the COPY lines of backend/Dockerfile and frontend/Dockerfile and the files
# those builds read: npm ci needs the root lockfile and all three workspace
# manifests, the backend build needs tsconfig.json + src + prisma, the frontend
# build needs tsconfig.json, next.config.ts, postcss.config.mjs, eslint.config.mjs,
# src and public. A directory needs both its own entry and its `/**` entry, and
# a `!` entry only survives what comes after it, so the secret excludes below
# stay a second layer that prunes inside the allow list (nothing here ships a
# .env at all, so `.env.example` is not excepted: no Dockerfile copies it).
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json

!backend/package.json
!backend/tsconfig.json
!backend/prisma
!backend/prisma/**
!backend/src
!backend/src/**

!frontend/package.json
!frontend/tsconfig.json
!frontend/next.config.ts
!frontend/postcss.config.mjs
!frontend/eslint.config.mjs
!frontend/public
!frontend/public/**
!frontend/src
!frontend/src/**

!mcp/package.json

# Second layer: keep secrets and host-built artifacts out even under an entry
# above (they are matched anywhere in the tree, so a key committed inside a
# source directory stays out of the context too).
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.npmrc
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
